---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '~/config/site.config';
const email = siteConfig.org.contactEmail;
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How makepicsmall handles your data. Short answer: we don't. Compression happens entirely in your browser; your files never leave your device.">
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: 2026-04-22</p>
  <div class="prose prose-slate mt-6 max-w-none">
    <p>
      <strong>Short version:</strong> makepicsmall is a browser-based image
      compressor. Your images are compressed on your own device using
      WebAssembly. <strong>We never upload, store, or transmit the images
      you drop into the tool.</strong> There is no server to send them to.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We do not upload your images anywhere. Compression runs 100% in your browser.</li>
      <li>We do not require an account, email, or login.</li>
      <li>We do not use advertising cookies or cross-site trackers.</li>
      <li>We do not sell, rent, or share any data about you.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What is collected automatically</h2>
    <p>
      makepicsmall is served through <strong>Cloudflare</strong>, which acts
      as our CDN. When your browser requests a page from
      <code>makepicsmall.com</code>, Cloudflare processes standard HTTP
      request metadata — your IP address, user-agent string, referring URL,
      and the path requested — in order to serve the page and protect the
      site from abuse. Cloudflare retains this metadata per
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">their own privacy policy</a>.
      We do not have access to identifiable logs from Cloudflare beyond
      aggregate traffic counts.
    </p>
    <p>
      We plan to enable <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> (or
      Plausible) for aggregate, privacy-preserving traffic measurement.
      Both set no cookies and do not identify individual users.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      makepicsmall does not set any first-party cookies. If a third-party
      analytics provider is enabled in the future, it will be a
      cookie-less provider.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights (GDPR, UK GDPR, PIPEDA, CCPA)</h2>
    <p>
      Because we do not collect personal data tied to you, there is
      generally nothing on our side to access, export, correct, or delete.
      If you believe we hold information about you and you want to exercise
      a right under GDPR, UK GDPR, PIPEDA, or CCPA — including the right
      of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection, or
      portability — email us at
      <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> and we will respond within
      30 days.
    </p>
    <p>
      You also have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data
      protection authority (for EU residents, your national DPA; for UK
      residents, the ICO; for Canadians, the Office of the Privacy
      Commissioner).
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      The service is not directed at children under 13. We knowingly
      collect no information from children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy as the site evolves. The "last updated"
      date at the top of this page will always reflect the most recent
      revision.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Privacy questions: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
